{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And also the priests who draw near to YHWH.</b> Through the offerings. The firstborn were called priests, for the service was among the firstborn. Or one may interpret 'the priests' as the sons of Aharon literally, and they were called priests on account of the future, for the priesthood was destined to be given to them; and like it (Genesis 2:14): ״הוא ההולך קדמת אשור״ — which is called Ashur on account of the future." "<b>Let them sanctify themselves.</b> And from this it is written (Leviticus 10:3) ״בקרובי אקדש״ — He said ״בקרובי״ corresponding to ״הנגשים״ (who draw near), and He said ״אקדש״ corresponding to ״יתקדשו״ (let them sanctify themselves)." "<b>Lest YHWH break forth among them.</b> This alludes to their death, that YHWH would break forth among them, but He did not wish to punish them now at the giving of the Torah, so as not to intermix the joy of the Torah, and He waited for them until the eighth day of the inauguration (milu'im). And it says ״וגםם — also — to include the seventy elders."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The opening phrase 'על ידי הקרבנות' appears to explain how the priests 'draw near' — through offering sacrifices — though its syntactic placement after the lemma is terse and slightly detached."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:14.755529877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}